# Phase 28: without this file, `COPY . .` in the Dockerfile bakes
# whatever happens to be sitting in the build context into the image layer
# -- including a real local .env (if one exists on the machine running
# `docker build`) and the database dump files scripts/db_backup.sh writes
# to backups/ (see backend/.gitignore's own Phase 28 addition for the same
# reason). Both would ship real secrets/user data inside the image, which
# is very different from a stray dev file: an image can be pushed to a
# registry, pulled elsewhere, and inspected layer-by-layer long after the
# container that built it is gone.
.env
.env.*
!.env.example
backups/
*.dump

.venv/
venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
.mypy_cache/
htmlcov/
.coverage

.git/
.gitignore

# Local dev-only storage fallback (app.core.storage's STORAGE_LOCAL_DIR
# default) -- never something a built image should carry.
storage/

*.md
